WEBVTT

00:00:00.577 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.764 --> 00:00:06.491
In this lesson, we do a basic relaxation massage, focusing on the back,

00:00:06.441 --> 00:00:08.270
the shoulders and the legs,

00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:09.310
step by step.

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:12.990
For timing and sequence, follow your salon's treatment.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.910
Keep these things in mind throughout:

00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:18.777
ask before you work, uncover only the area you are working on,

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.510
and keep the pressure pleasant,

00:00:20.698 --> 00:00:21.550
never painful.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:22.999
Step one:

00:00:23.165 --> 00:00:24.119
prepare the room.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.039
The room is warm and quiet.

00:00:26.314 --> 00:00:29.319
Wipe and disinfect the bed surface and the face cradle.

00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:33.550
Lay a clean sheet, a fresh face cradle cover, a large towel,

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.239
and a bolster for the legs.

00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:37.159
The oil is in a pump bottle.

00:00:37.461 --> 00:00:40.839
Adjust the bed height to suit you, so you can work without bending over.

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:42.283
Step two:

00:00:42.532 --> 00:00:43.483
the consultation.

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:49.384
Ask about health, medication, oil and nut allergies, recent injuries or surgery,

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.603
and any areas the client does not want massaged.

00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:55.643
If you see varicose veins, don't press on them.

00:00:55.982 --> 00:00:59.609
If you see one calf swollen, red and warm, don't massage,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.683
and advise the client to see a doctor right away.

00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:06.878
Then explain to the client how the draping works, what the pressure will be like,

00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:09.083
and that they can ask you to stop at any time.

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:10.528
Step three:

00:01:10.777 --> 00:01:12.368
the client undresses alone.

00:01:12.546 --> 00:01:13.328
You step out.

00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:16.977
Ask the client to lie face down, face in the face cradle,

00:01:16.927 --> 00:01:19.648
with the large towel pulled up to the shoulders.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:21.648
The client may keep their underwear on.

00:01:21.997 --> 00:01:25.168
Knock, wait for an answer, and only then come in.

00:01:25.436 --> 00:01:28.688
Wash your hands with soap, dry them, and rub them warm.

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:30.205
Step four:

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:31.005
draping.

00:01:31.437 --> 00:01:34.765
Fold the towel down to the waist, uncovering only the back.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.125
Tuck the edges of the towel securely on both sides.

00:01:38.472 --> 00:01:42.285
If the client wishes, place a small bolster under the ankles for comfort.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:43.565
Ask the client:

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:44.765
are you warm enough?

00:01:45.181 --> 00:01:48.205
If they are cold, the muscles find it hard to relax.

00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:49.646
Step five:

00:01:49.902 --> 00:01:51.806
the oil, and the first touch.

00:01:52.238 --> 00:01:55.726
Pump a little oil into your palm, and warm it between your hands.

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.766
Never pour oil straight onto the client's back.

00:01:59.195 --> 00:02:03.486
Place both hands on the back very gently, and hold still for a moment.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:08.046
From now on, whenever you change movements, always keep a hand on the client.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.585
Step six:

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.425
long strokes on the back.

00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:15.967
Both palms move up from the lower back, on either side of the spine,

00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:18.705
to the shoulders, then sweep out to the sides,

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.385
and glide lightly back down.

00:02:20.863 --> 00:02:25.148
Work slowly, about three to five times, gradually increasing the pressure,

00:02:25.098 --> 00:02:27.665
so the muscles warm up before you go deeper.

00:02:28.173 --> 00:02:31.985
Stand in a lunge, use your body weight, and keep your back straight.

00:02:32.412 --> 00:02:33.425
Then ask the client:

00:02:33.669 --> 00:02:34.785
is this pressure okay?

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.233
Step seven:

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:37.753
knead the shoulders.

00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:41.718
The muscle on top of the shoulders, between the neck and the shoulder,

00:02:41.668 --> 00:02:42.953
is usually the tightest.

00:02:43.332 --> 00:02:47.839
Gently lift the muscle between your thumb and fingers, and knead slowly,

00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:48.953
in an even rhythm.

00:02:49.248 --> 00:02:51.433
No hard squeezing, no pinching.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.753
Ask the client about the pressure again.

00:02:54.404 --> 00:02:56.244
The nape and the back of the neck:

00:02:56.746 --> 00:03:00.783
use your fingertips to stroke lightly from the hairline down to the shoulders,

00:03:00.733 --> 00:03:02.164
on either side of the neck.

00:03:02.673 --> 00:03:05.924
On the neck, the pressure is always lighter than on the back.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:10.404
Don't press on the front of the neck, and never twist or crack the client's neck.

00:03:10.672 --> 00:03:12.964
That is not part of relaxation massage.

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:14.330
Step eight:

00:03:14.587 --> 00:03:18.970
thumb circles, around the shoulder blades, and along both sides of the spine.

00:03:19.389 --> 00:03:21.290
Never press on the spine itself.

00:03:21.639 --> 00:03:25.370
Over the lower back, near the kidneys, only stroke lightly;

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:27.690
no pounding, no hard tapping.

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.812
When you find a tight spot, slow down, and stay a little longer,

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:35.290
rather than pressing harder than the client finds comfortable.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:39.679
Then, tap lightly if the client likes it, finish with a few long strokes,

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:41.050
and cover the back again.

00:03:41.715 --> 00:03:42.577
Step nine:

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.097
the backs of the legs.

00:03:44.561 --> 00:03:48.281
Uncover only a single leg, from the ankle to above the knee,

00:03:48.231 --> 00:03:50.177
and tuck the towel in securely.

00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:52.257
The other leg stays fully covered.

00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:56.257
Stroke from the ankle up toward the knee, that is, toward the heart.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:04:01.457
Knead the calf gently, hands alternating, lifting the muscle and releasing it.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:03.457
Avoid the hollow behind the knee.

00:04:03.636 --> 00:04:05.297
Don't press on raised veins.

00:04:05.452 --> 00:04:09.457
When you are done, cover the leg, and only then uncover the other one.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.740
Step ten:

00:04:11.046 --> 00:04:11.860
turning over.

00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:16.622
Lift the towel just enough, holding the far side firmly against the bed,

00:04:16.572 --> 00:04:19.220
and keep your eyes toward the client's face.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.580
Ask the client to turn onto their back, under the towel.

00:04:23.007 --> 00:04:24.980
The client stays covered the whole time.

00:04:25.447 --> 00:04:27.620
Place a bolster under the knees if they wish.

00:04:28.049 --> 00:04:31.540
If the treatment includes the fronts of the legs, work as on the backs:

00:04:31.873 --> 00:04:35.659
uncover a single leg, stroke from the ankle up toward the knee,

00:04:35.609 --> 00:04:37.380
don't press on the shin bone,

00:04:37.536 --> 00:04:38.820
and avoid the inner thigh.

00:04:39.473 --> 00:04:40.266
Step eleven:

00:04:40.607 --> 00:04:41.946
arms and shoulders.

00:04:42.203 --> 00:04:44.586
Uncover an arm, and rest it on the towel.

00:04:44.789 --> 00:04:47.226
One hand holds the client's wrist lightly;

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:50.826
the other strokes from the wrist up to the elbow, toward the heart.

00:04:51.087 --> 00:04:52.026
Avoid the armpit.

00:04:52.285 --> 00:04:54.266
Cover it again, and do the other arm.

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:58.213
Then move to the head of the bed, place both hands on the shoulders,

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:00.346
and press down lightly for a few breaths.

00:05:00.937 --> 00:05:01.798
Step twelve:

00:05:02.059 --> 00:05:02.758
the finish.

00:05:03.656 --> 00:05:06.424
Rest your hands on the client's shoulders for a moment,

00:05:06.374 --> 00:05:08.598
then gently let them know you have finished.

00:05:08.933 --> 00:05:12.758
Step out, so the client can sit up slowly, and get dressed.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.798
Offer a glass of water, and ask how they feel.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:16.678
Tell them:

00:05:17.105 --> 00:05:20.918
they may feel slightly sore the next day, especially after firm pressure.

00:05:21.265 --> 00:05:24.998
If there is a lot of pain, or bruising, let the salon know.

00:05:25.178 --> 00:05:28.838
Write it in the internal notes on the client record in VaraaAi:

00:05:29.192 --> 00:05:33.078
the pressure they like, the areas to avoid, and the oil used.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.734
There are a few very common mistakes that clients remember for a long time.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.014
Pouring cold oil straight onto the client's back.

00:05:41.523 --> 00:05:44.614
Lifting both hands off, then putting them back suddenly.

00:05:45.208 --> 00:05:47.814
Uncovering more than the area you are working on.

00:05:48.122 --> 00:05:49.334
Pressing on the spine.

00:05:49.842 --> 00:05:52.454
Talking all the time when the client wants to rest.

00:05:52.961 --> 00:05:54.694
And forgetting to ask about pressure.

00:05:54.986 --> 00:05:59.414
Just avoid these mistakes, and the client will already see you as very professional.

00:06:00.079 --> 00:06:01.111
Step thirteen:

00:06:01.233 --> 00:06:01.911
clean up.

00:06:02.236 --> 00:06:06.631
Sheets, towels and face cradle covers go into a laundry basket with a lid.

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:09.511
Wipe and disinfect the bed and the face cradle.

00:06:09.849 --> 00:06:10.951
Wipe the oil bottle.

00:06:11.218 --> 00:06:12.311
Then wash your hands.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.431
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
